## Web app

The web app is a [Vue](https://vuejs.org) single-page app in TypeScript in
`frontend/`, created by `npm create vite@{{index .NPM "create-vite"}}` with
the `vue-ts` template and built with [Vite](https://vite.dev). Its example
page lists the items of the JSON API under `{{.APIPrefix}}/` and adds new ones.
It needs [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) {{.Node}} (the version CI and the image
use) or another release that the scaffolded packages support.

The Go binary embeds the build from `{{.Slots.web.Dir}}/dist/app` and serves it at
`/`, with `index.html` for every path without a file extension, so
client-side routes survive a reload. Until the frontend is built, `/` shows
how to build it; `go build` and `go test` work without Node.js.

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make build` | Installs (`npm ci`) and builds the frontend, then builds the binary |
| `make dev` | Runs the Vite dev server on <http://localhost:5173>, which forwards `{{.APIPrefix}}` to the Go server; run `make run` next to it |
| `npm --prefix frontend run build` | Builds the frontend only; then `go run ./{{.Slots.entry.Dir}}` serves it |

The page is in `frontend/src/App.vue`, its API client in `frontend/src/api.ts`,
and its styles in `frontend/src/style.css`. `frontend/vite.config.ts` sets the
build output and the dev server's proxy. `frontend/package-lock.json` pins
every npm dependency; Dependabot keeps them current.
